\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj It works with anything comparable \u8212? text and {\f1\fs18 Enum} values included. {\b The expression after {\f1\fs18\b Select Case} is evaluated exactly once}, which for {\f1\fs18 Select Case NextNumber()} is the difference between one call and one per branch.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Loops\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Dim i As Integer\line 
For i = 1 To 10\line 
    Print i\line 
Next i\line 
\line 
For i = 10 To 1 Step -1\line 
    Print i\line 
Next i\line 
\line 
For i As Integer = 1 To 3     ' declared here, valid only in the loop\line 
    Print i\line 
Next i\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Start, end and step are evaluated {\b once}, before the first pass. If the step is only known at run time, its sign decides the direction \u8212? {\f1\fs18 Step direction} works. The name after {\f1\fs18 Next} is optional; if present it must match.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 For Each} runs over arrays and over anything {\f1\fs18 Iterable} \u8212? that is, every Java collection:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Dim fruit As String\line 
For Each fruit In list\line 
    Print fruit\line 
Next fruit\line 
\line 
For Each s As String In list     ' or say it right here\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj If the variable was declared beforehand, its type applies. Otherwise it comes from the sequence: for an array the element type, for a collection {\f1\fs18 Object}, because generics are erased.\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 While supply > 0\line 
    Take()\line 
Wend\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 End While} works as well; {\f1\fs18 Wend} is the VB6 spelling, and both close the same loop.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 Do ... Loop} has five shapes, and the difference is {\i when} the test happens:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Do While condition      Do Until condition      Do\line 
    ...                     ...                     ...\line 
Loop                    Loop                    Loop While condition\line 
\line 
Do                      Do\line 
    ...                     ...\line 
Loop Until condition    Loop            ' endless, left with Exit Do\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 Until c} means {\f1\fs18 While Not c}. The two shapes that test at the end run at least once.\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 For i = 1 To 100\line 
    If i = 3 Then Continue For     ' next round\line 
    If i > 10 Then Exit For        ' leave the loop\line 
    Print i\line 
Next i\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 Exit For}, {\f1\fs18 Exit Do} and {\f1\fs18 Exit While} leave the loop; {\f1\fs18 Exit Sub} and {\f1\fs18 Exit Function} leave the procedure.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 With\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Saves the receiver and evaluates it {\b once}:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 With window\line 
    .setSize(400, 300)\line 
    .Title = "tsbRapidFX"\line 
    .Visible = True\line 
End With\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj With {\f1\fs18 With list(i)} the indexing happens once, however many members the block touches. A leading dot outside a {\f1\fs18 With} is a clear error ({\f1\fs18 RFX0711}).\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 GoTo and labels\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Dim i As Integer = 0\line 
Again:\line 
    i += 1\line 
    If i < 3 Then GoTo Again\line 
\line 
    If done Then GoTo Finished\line 
    Print "work"\line 
Finished:\line 
    Print "done"\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A label is a name with a colon at the start of a statement. Jumps go forwards and backwards but only within the same procedure; an unknown label reports {\f1\fs18 RFX1002}. {\f1\fs18 GoTo} exists mainly because {\f1\fs18 On Error GoTo} needs it. A jump out of a {\f1\fs18 Try ... Finally} runs the {\f1\fs18 Finally} first.\par
\pard\sb160\sa160\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb400\sa140\f2\b\fs34\cf2 5 Procedures, lambdas and AddressOf\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Sub and Function\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Sub Greet(name As String)\line 
    Print "Hello, " + name\line 
End Sub\line 
\line 
Function Square(x As Integer) As Integer\line 
    Return x * x\line 
End Function\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Both are called the same way; writing {\f1\fs18 Call} in front is allowed and unnecessary. {\b The order in the source is irrelevant} \u8212? a procedure may call one declared further down. If a {\f1\fs18 Function} runs off the end without a {\f1\fs18 Return}, it returns its type's default.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Parameters\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\b {\f1\fs18\b ByVal} is the default.} The procedure gets a copy; assignments to it stay inside. For reference types the {\i reference} is copied, not the object \u8212? so {\f1\fs18 list.add(...)} inside is visible outside, {\f1\fs18 list = New ArrayList()} is not.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\b {\f1\fs18\b ByRef} lets the caller see the change:}\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Sub Swap(ByRef a As Integer, ByRef b As Integer)\line 
    Dim h As Integer = a\line 
    a = b\line 
    b = h\line 
End Sub\line 
\line 
Dim x As Integer = 1\line 
Dim y As Integer = 2\line 
Swap(x, y)\line 
Print x + " " + y      ' 2 1\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\li360\ri200\sb140\sa180\sl276\slmult1\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw40\brdrcf5\brsp120\f0\fs20\cf1 {\b {\f1\fs18\b ByRef} only works when the call is a statement of its own.} The JVM passes everything by value, so a {\f1\fs18 ByRef} travels in a one-element array and the call expands into copy-in, call, copy-out. Copy-out is a statement, and there is no room for one in the middle of an expression. {\f1\fs18 Dim s = "" + Increase(x)} therefore reports {\f1\fs18 RFX0712} \u8212? better a message than a silently lost change.\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\b {\f1\fs18\b Optional} with a default:}\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Function Greeting(name As String, Optional word As String = "Hello") As String\line 
    Return word + ", " + name\line 
End Function\line 
\line 
Print Greeting("World")              ' Hello, World\line 
Print Greeting("World", "Hi")        ' Hi, World\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj The default must be a constant and is inserted {\b at the call site}. After one {\f1\fs18 Optional}, all further parameters must be optional too ({\f1\fs18 RFX0710}).\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\b {\f1\fs18\b ParamArray} takes any number:}\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Function Total(ParamArray values As Integer()) As Integer\line 
    Dim sum As Integer = 0\line 
    Dim w As Integer\line 
    For Each w In values\line 
        sum += w\line 
    Next w\line 
    Return sum\line 
End Function\line 
\line 
Print Total()              ' 0\line 
Print Total(1, 2, 3)       ' 6\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Only on the last parameter, and its type must be an array.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Overloading\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Several procedures may share a name as long as their parameter types differ. Which one is meant is decided by the same rules as for Java methods: first without boxing, then with, then with {\f1\fs18 ParamArray}, and within a stage the most specific wins. Two declarations that would be the same method after compiling report {\f1\fs18 RFX0706}.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Lambdas\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A lambda is a procedure without a name, written where a value is expected:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Dim r As Runnable = Sub() Print "running"\line 
r.run()\line 
\line 
Dim f As java.util.function.IntUnaryOperator = Function(x) x * 2\line 
Print f.applyAsInt(4)          ' 8\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Multi-line, even inside an argument list:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 list.forEach(Sub(x)\line 
    Print "  - " + x\line 
End Sub)\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\b Parameter types need not be written.} They come from the interface the lambda is being placed into \u8212? which is why {\f1\fs18 btn.addActionListener(Sub(e) ...)} never names {\f1\fs18 ActionEvent}. You {\i may} write them.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A lambda fits anywhere a {\b single-method interface} is expected: {\f1\fs18 Runnable}, {\f1\fs18 ActionListener}, {\f1\fs18 Comparator}, {\f1\fs18 Consumer}, and equally one you declared yourself. It has no type of its own; standing where nothing says what it should become \u8212? {\f1\fs18 Dim x = Sub() ...} \u8212? reports {\f1\fs18 RFX0800}.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A lambda may read what surrounds it: locals, fields, {\f1\fs18 Me}.\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Public Class Counter\line 
    Private state As Integer\line 
\line 
    Public Sub Register(button As JButton)\line 
        button.addActionListener(Sub(e)\line 
            state += 1                    ' a field of this instance\line 
            Print "State: " + state\line 
        End Sub)\line 
    End Sub\line 
End Class\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Under the hood the body becomes an ordinary static method of the enclosing class, captured values become its first parameters, and the call site keeps an {\f1\fs18 invokedynamic} through the {\f1\fs18 LambdaMetafactory} \u8212? the same shape javac produces, so the JVM optimises both alike. {\b No extra class file is created per lambda.}\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 AddressOf\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Places an existing procedure where an interface is expected \u8212? VB's spelling of Java's {\f1\fs18 this::method}:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 list.forEach(AddressOf Show)\line 
button.addActionListener(AddressOf Handle)\line 
\line 
Sub Show(value As Object)\line 
    Print value\line 
End Sub\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj It works for module procedures, for methods of your own class (and then {\f1\fs18 Me} travels with it), and for Java methods. {\b {\f1\fs18\b AddressOf} on a private instance method is what makes the form designers possible}: it carries {\f1\fs18 Me}, so a generated {\f1\fs18 button.addActionListener(AddressOf OnClick)} can reach every field of the form while the body of {\f1\fs18 OnClick} stays entirely yours.\par
\pard\sb160\sa160\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb400\sa140\f2\b\fs34\cf2 6 Your own types\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Five kinds, and each becomes a real class file \u8212? an ordinary type as seen from Java.\par
