\pard\plain\intbl\sb20\sa20\f0\fs19\cf1\b0 the method has no body; every inheriting class must supply one\cell
\row
\trowd\trgaph80\trleft0\trpaddl80\trpaddr80\trpaddt40\trpaddb40
\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\cellx4790
\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\cellx9580
\pard\plain\intbl\sb20\sa20\f0\fs19\cf1\b0 {\f1\fs18 NotInheritable}\cell
\pard\plain\intbl\sb20\sa20\f0\fs19\cf1\b0 nobody inherits from this class\cell
\row
\pard\sb0\sa140

\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Calls dispatch dynamically. If the base class has no parameterless constructor, {\f1\fs18 MyBase.New(...)} must be written with arguments ({\f1\fs18 RFX0704}).\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Interface and Implements\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Public Interface IShape\line 
    Function Area() As Double\line 
    Function Name() As String\line 
End Interface\line 
\line 
Public Class Circle\line 
    Implements IShape\line 
\line 
    Private r As Double\line 
\line 
    Public Sub New(radius As Double)\line 
        r = radius\line 
    End Sub\line 
\line 
    Public Function Area() As Double\line 
        Return 3.14159 * r * r\line 
    End Function\line 
\line 
    Public Function Name() As String\line 
        Return "Circle"\line 
    End Function\line 
End Class\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Several interfaces are listed with commas or on several {\f1\fs18 Implements} lines. A missing method reports {\b {\f1\fs18\b RFX0713} at the class} \u8212? not later as a crash when somebody calls it.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\b Java interfaces too.} That is where tsbRapidFX code becomes usable {\i by} the JDK: implement {\f1\fs18 java.lang.Comparable} and {\f1\fs18 Collections.sort(list)} will sort a list of your own objects, calling back into tsbRapidFX code as it goes.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Properties\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Public Class Account\line 
    Private amount As Double\line 
\line 
    Public Property Balance As Double\line 
        Get\line 
            Return amount\line 
        End Get\line 
        Set(value As Double)\line 
            If value < 0 Then Throw New java.lang.IllegalArgumentException("negative")\line 
            amount = value\line 
        End Set\line 
    End Property\line 
End Class\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Used like a variable: {\f1\fs18 account.Balance = 100}. {\b Without a body you get an auto-property} \u8212? field and both accessors are generated:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Public Property Name As String\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Only a {\f1\fs18 Get} makes it read-only, only a {\f1\fs18 Set} write-only.\par
\pard\plain\li360\ri200\sb140\sa180\sl276\slmult1\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw40\brdrcf5\brsp120\f0\fs20\cf1 {\b A property becomes {\f1\fs18\b getX} and {\f1\fs18\b setX}.} That is not cosmetic: the same spelling that reads {\f1\fs18 btn.Text} on a Swing button reads a tsbRapidFX property, and Java sees a property where you wrote one.\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Enum\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Public Enum Colour\line 
    Red = 1\line 
    Green = 2\line 
    Blue = 4\line 
End Enum\line 
\line 
Public Enum Day\line 
    Monday        ' 0\line 
    Tuesday       ' 1\line 
    Wednesday     ' 2\line 
End Enum\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Without numbers it counts from zero; with numbers, what is written applies and the next one without a number continues from there.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A tsbRapidFX {\f1\fs18 Enum} is a {\b real {\f1\fs18\b java.lang.Enum}}:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Dim c As Colour = Colour.Green\line 
Print c                     ' Green - the name, not the number\line 
Print c.Value               ' 2     - the number after the =\line 
Print c.name()              ' Green\line 
Print Colour.valueOf("Red")\line 
\line 
Dim x As Colour\line 
For Each x In Colour.values()\line 
    Print x + " = " + x.Value\line 
Next x\line 
\line 
Dim m As java.util.EnumMap = New java.util.EnumMap(GetType(Colour))\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Structure\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A {\f1\fs18 Structure} is a {\b value}, not a reference:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Public Structure Point\line 
    Public X As Integer\line 
    Public Y As Integer\line 
\line 
    Public Function Length() As Double\line 
        Return Math.sqrt(X * X + Y * Y)\line 
    End Function\line 
End Structure\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Dim a As Point          ' already there, X = 0, Y = 0 - never Nothing\line 
a.X = 3\line 
a.Y = 4\line 
\line 
Dim b As Point = a      ' copied\line 
b.X = 99\line 
Print a                 ' Point(X=3, Y=4)\line 
Print b                 ' Point(X=99, Y=4)\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj What follows from that:\par
\pard\plain\fi-260\li520\sb0\sa90\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8226?\tab {\b Assigning copies}, and so does passing to a procedure. A change inside stays inside.\par
\pard\plain\fi-260\li520\sb0\sa90\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8226?\tab {\b {\f1\fs18\b =} compares the fields}, not identity. Two points with the same content are equal.\par
\pard\plain\fi-260\li520\sb0\sa90\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8226?\tab {\b Usable as a {\f1\fs18\b HashMap} key}, because {\f1\fs18 hashCode} matches {\f1\fs18 equals}.\par
\pard\plain\fi-260\li520\sb0\sa90\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8226?\tab {\b {\f1\fs18\b Print} shows the fields}: {\f1\fs18 Point(X=3, Y=4)}.\par
\pard\plain\fi-260\li520\sb0\sa90\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8226?\tab A {\f1\fs18 Structure} neither inherits nor is inherited from.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj The JVM has no value types; all of this is generated. The price is a copy on every hand-over \u8212? right for something small like a point, and a reason to use a {\f1\fs18 Class} for something large.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Visibility\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 Public}, {\f1\fs18 Private}, {\f1\fs18 Protected} and {\f1\fs18 Friend} are all read. {\f1\fs18 Private} is enforced on fields and methods; the rest is emitted public. Private means the class, not the family. Interface members are necessarily public \u8212? a private one could not be implemented and the JVM rejects it \u8212? and {\f1\fs18 AddressOf} on a private method of the same class keeps working, which is what every generated form relies on.\par
\pard\sb160\sa160\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb400\sa140\f2\b\fs34\cf2 7 Error handling\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj There are two routes. {\f1\fs18 Try/Catch} is the one to use; {\f1\fs18 On Error} is there for code coming from VB6. Both fill the same {\f1\fs18 Err}, so that the language does not have two error objects.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Try ... Catch\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Try\line 
    Dim n As Integer = CInt(input)\line 
    Print "Number: " + n\line 
Catch e As java.lang.IllegalArgumentException\line 
    Print "That was not a number."\line 
End Try\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Several branches are tested {\b in the order written}; the first match wins, so the more specific type belongs on top. A {\f1\fs18 Catch} without a type catches {\f1\fs18 Exception}.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj An {\f1\fs18 Error} \u8212? {\f1\fs18 OutOfMemoryError}, {\f1\fs18 StackOverflowError} \u8212? is {\b not} caught. That is deliberate: a program cannot sensibly handle one, and swallowing it turns a crash into a hang.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 When\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A branch may add a condition on top of the type:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Try\line 
    Process(file)\line 
Catch e As java.io.IOException When file.Name.endsWith(".tmp")\line 
    Print "Temporary file - skipped"\line 
Catch e As java.io.IOException\line 
    Throw\line 
End Try\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj If the condition says no, {\b the next branch is tried}, not rethrown.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Finally\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Runs on every way out of the block \u8212? after the normal end, after any {\f1\fs18 Catch}, on a {\f1\fs18 Return}, on an {\f1\fs18 Exit For}, and when the error carries on outwards.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A {\f1\fs18 Try} needs at least one {\f1\fs18 Catch} or one {\f1\fs18 Finally} ({\f1\fs18 RFX1000}) \u8212? otherwise it would do nothing.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Throw\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Throw New java.lang.IllegalArgumentException("amount must not be negative")\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A {\f1\fs18 Throw} with no argument inside a {\f1\fs18 Catch} passes the caught error on unchanged. Only something below {\f1\fs18 java.lang.Throwable} can be thrown ({\f1\fs18 RFX1001}).\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Using\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Closes a resource however the block is left:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Using reader As java.io.BufferedReader = _\line 
        New java.io.BufferedReader(New java.io.FileReader(path))\line 
    Print reader.readLine()\line 
End Using\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj That is a {\f1\fs18 Try ... Finally} you do not have to write and therefore cannot forget. The type needs a {\f1\fs18 close()} ({\f1\fs18 RFX1006}); every {\f1\fs18 java.lang.AutoCloseable} qualifies, and so does a class of your own as soon as it has such a method. {\f1\fs18 Using} is the natural shape for a JDBC connection \u8212? see Chapter 12.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Err\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Try\line 
    Err.Raise(513, "Import", "line unreadable")\line 
Catch e As Exception\line 
    Print Err.Number          ' 513\line 
    Print Err.Description     ' line unreadable\line 
    Print Err.Source          ' Import\line 
End Try\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
