\pard\sb0\sa140

\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 Err} is per thread. Two threads failing at once do not read each other's errors.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 On Error \u8212? the VB6 shape\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 Sub Load()\line 
    On Error GoTo Failure\line 
\line 
    Dim content As String = ReadAllText("/tmp/data.txt")\line 
    Process(content)\line 
    Exit Sub\line 
\line 
Failure:\line 
    Print "Error " + Err.Number + ": " + Err.Description\line 
End Sub\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj From the {\f1\fs18 On Error GoTo} line onwards every error jumps to the named label. Two restrictions, both reported: the label must sit {\b directly in the method body}, not inside a block ({\f1\fs18 RFX1004}), and there is {\b one target per method} ({\f1\fs18 RFX1003}). {\f1\fs18 On Error GoTo 0} switches handling off again.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 On Error Resume Next} protects each following statement individually; a failure is recorded and the next statement runs. {\f1\fs18 Resume} inside a handler does not exist ({\f1\fs18 RFX0900}).\par
\pard\sb160\sa160\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb400\sa140\f2\b\fs34\cf2 8 The standard library\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj All of the following are available {\b without a prefix} \u8212? no {\f1\fs18 Imports} needed.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj They are not language constructs but static methods in the runtime jar that the compiler keeps in scope. Two things follow: overloads like {\f1\fs18 Mid(s, 2)} and {\f1\fs18 Mid(s, 2, 3)} work like any Java method's, and {\b a function of your own with the same name hides the library's} \u8212? the same rule a local has against a field.\par
\pard\plain\li360\ri200\sb140\sa180\sl276\slmult1\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw40\brdrcf5\brsp120\f0\fs20\cf1 {\b The dollar sign is decoration.} {\f1\fs18 Left$} and {\f1\fs18 Left} are the same function. In VB the {\f1\fs18 $} form returned a {\f1\fs18 String} and the other a {\f1\fs18 Variant}; in a statically typed language that is one and the same thing, but ported code writes the dollar.\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Strings\par
