\pard\plain\li360\ri200\sb140\sa180\sl276\slmult1\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw40\brdrcf5\brsp120\f0\fs20\cf1 {\b Positions count from zero, and "not found" is -1.} That is Java's rule, not VB's, and it is deliberate: {\f1\fs18 InStr} and {\f1\fs18 indexOf} answer with the same number on the same string, {\f1\fs18 Mid} and {\f1\fs18 substring} likewise. So our functions and the JDK's mix without any +/-1 anywhere \u8212? and in a language that sits entirely on Java, that mixing happens constantly. {\b Going out of range is not an error.} {\f1\fs18 Left("Hello", 99)} is {\f1\fs18 "Hello"}, {\f1\fs18 Mid} past the end is {\f1\fs18 ""}. VB never threw here.\par
