\pard\plain\keepn\sb400\sa140\f2\b\fs34\cf2 20 SessionStatic: the mechanism, the measurements, the rule\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 The problem it removes\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A {\f1\fs18 Shared} field in a multi-user server is the classic data leak: one user's number sits where every other user's code can read it, and {\b nothing about writing it looks wrong}. The usual advice \u8212? "do not use statics on a server" \u8212? asks people to remember a rule at every declaration, which is a rule they will forget once and never find again.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\f1\fs18 SessionStatic} removes the choice rather than restating the rule.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 How it is built\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A field declared {\f1\fs18 SessionStatic} {\b is not a JVM field at all.}\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj That sentence is the whole design. The emitter walks the fields of a type and skips it:\par
\pard\plain\li260\ri200\sb120\sa160\sl240\slmult1\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf4\brsp40\cbpat3\f1\fs17\cf1 // A SessionStatic gets no slot at all. That absence is the feature: with no field\line 
// there is nothing for one user's value to sit in where another user's code can\line 
// reach it, so the isolation cannot be undone by forgetting.\line 
if (field.isSessionStatic()) continue;\par
\pard\sb0\sa0\cbpat0\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj Instead, every read becomes a call and every write becomes a call:\par
\trowd\trgaph80\trleft0\trpaddl80\trpaddr80\trpaddt40\trpaddb40
\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clcbpat6\cellx4790
\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clcbpat6\cellx9580
\pard\plain\intbl\sb20\sa20\f0\fs19\cf1\b Source\cell
\pard\plain\intbl\sb20\sa20\f0\fs19\cf1\b Bytecode\cell
\row
\trowd\trgaph80\trleft0\trpaddl80\trpaddr80\trpaddt40\trpaddb40
\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\cellx4790
\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf4\cellx9580
\pard\plain\intbl\sb20\sa20\f0\fs19\cf1\b0 {\f1\fs18 Counter} (read)\cell
\pard\plain\intbl\sb20\sa20\f0\fs19\cf1\b0 {\f1\fs18 LDC "Main.Counter"} \u183? {\f1\fs18 INVOKESTATIC RfxSessionStatics.getInt}\cell
\row
