\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj A component is a specification \u8212? a class name, a default size, a render key, an attachment strategy and a list of property descriptors. Properties come in bundles along the Swing class hierarchy, so adding a control is {\b one entry} in the catalogue, not a new file.\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj {\b SmartTable} in that list is {\f1\fs18 tsbSmartTable} from Chapter 17, and it is the only table whose column widths the designer can set.\par
\pard\plain\keepn\sb280\sa100\f2\b\fs26\cf1 Three containers, deliberately\par
\pard\plain\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21\cf1\qj The JavaFX designer this one descends from had sixteen. A stack pane, a split pane, a tabbed pane, two kinds of box and two kinds of grid mostly offer ways to be undecided. What a form needs is a page you can place things on freely, and a couple of panels to drop onto it:\par
